# XCU sh-errors
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1/Shell language syntax error
class      required
says       A syntax error makes a non-interactive shell write a diagnostic
           and exit with a non-zero status without running later commands.
test       t/001-syntax-error.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1/Special built-in utility error
class      required
says       An error in a special built-in run directly makes a non-
           interactive shell exit with a non-zero status: an invalid option
           to set, unsetting a read-only variable, giving export a value for
           a read-only variable.
test       t/002-special-builtin-exit.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1/executed via the
class      required
says       The same errors do not end the shell when the special built-in is
           run through the command utility.
test       t/003-special-via-command.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1/Other utility
class      required
says       An error in a utility that is not a special built-in does not end
           the shell.
test       t/004-other-utility-continues.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1/Redirection error with<br>
class      required
says       A failing redirection on a compound command, on a function call
           or on a regular utility does not end the shell; the command is
           not run and its status is non-zero.
test       t/006-redirect-others-continue.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.008
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1/Expansion error
class      required
says       An expansion error (an unset parameter with ${name?}, ${name:?},
           or an invalid expansion operator) makes a non-interactive shell
           exit with a non-zero status and a diagnostic.
test       t/008-expansion-error-exit.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.009
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1/occur in a subshell
class      required
says       An error that would end a shell ends only the subshell it happens
           in; the shell goes on with a non-zero status for the subshell.
test       t/009-subshell-errors.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.010
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
class      required
says       An interactive shell does not exit for a syntax error, a special
           built-in error, a redirection error of a special built-in, a
           variable assignment error, an expansion error, or an unknown
           command; later commands still run.
test       t/010-interactive-continues.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.011
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1/an interactive shell shall not perform any further processing
class      required
says       After an error that an interactive shell survives, it does not
           run the rest of the command in which the error happened.
test       t/011-interactive-abandons-command.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-errors.012
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.2
class      required
says       Command status values: 127 when the command is not found, 126
           when found but not executable; for a command ended by a signal,
           above 128; otherwise the exit value.
test       t/012-status-values.sh
